              "revision_30s": "Constitutional posts/bodies are created directly by the Constitution (need amendment to alter), unlike statutory bodies. President (Art 52-62, Electoral College, impeachment under Art 61); Governor (Art 153-162, pleasure of President, no fixed tenure); CAG (Art 148-151, removed like SC judge, reports to legislature); Attorney General (Art 76); ECI (Art 324, CEC removed like SC judge); UPSC (Art 315-323, 6-yr/65-yr tenure). Recent flashpoints: Anoop Baranwal (2023) on ECI appointment, Governor's discretionary powers on bill assent.",
