                "Codified rule-based ethical guidance for Indian civil servants includes instruments such as the Central Civil Services (Conduct) Rules, 1964 and equivalent All India Services conduct rules.",
                "The 2nd ARC's 4th Report emphasised that laws and rules alone cannot guarantee ethical governance without an internalised ethical value system among officials.",
                "Legal positivism (law as the sole valid standard of conduct) and natural-law/virtue-based approaches (a moral standard above enacted law) represent the two poles of this philosophical debate.",
                "Conscience-guided discretion is legitimate only when accompanied by transparency and willingness to be held accountable for the departure — it is not a substitute for due process."
