              "revision_30s": "Rules = codified, external, predictable but incomplete; conscience = internal moral compass that fills gaps rules cannot cover. Rigid rule-following without conscience risks 'bureaucratic apathy' (cf. Arendt). Conscience-guided discretion must still be transparent and accountable, not arbitrary. Indian anchor: 2nd ARC 4th Report — ethical governance needs internalised values, not rules alone.",
